  "result": {
    "summary": "Exact replay verified all 6912 saved warmup rows and 6912 paired evaluation rows across three seeds and endpoints128/512 with zero new environment hands. Endpoint512 pooled deltas were +3.902,+16.414,+10.247 and holdout was positive in2/3, but candidate-path flip rates were only0.804%,0.763%,0.842%; seed2 seat1 had only8 flip-hands. Only21-28/1152 hands per seed carried nonzero paired outcomes. Full suite:294 passed.",
    "conclusion": "The internal geometric improvement is real on its saved decks but is supported by extremely sparse, high-variance argmax-boundary events rather than broad policy improvement. This explains why preservation remained high and why a fresh5k external probe had little power to isolate the contextual effect. The preregistered action-support gate fails, so neither unchanged scaling nor a margin-only amplification of this proxy is warranted. This is a mechanism-specific pivot, not a claim that contextual or long-horizon learning is impossible.",
    "decision": "PIVOT_FROM_CURRENT_CONTEXT_PROXY_SPARSE_ARGMAX_SUPPORT",
    "next_step": "Return to a materially different learned-policy objective with denser all-action credit and real opponent-league/self-play hands. Before allocating a geometric 65k-to1m curve, audit primary AlphaHoldem training details against the current trainer and use existing multi-seed evidence to preregister one bounded causal control whose update signal is dense, source-preserving, and measured across six training identities, three SHA-disjoint holdouts, both seats, and all streets."
  },
